moval Risk Assessment.","fn_3139cc46":"The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","fn_36a21eec":"The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","fn_522810e2":"A population census in 2021, resulted in a revision of the number of persons under international protection living in Canada, which was previously estimated by UNHCR. Year-end stock refers to protected persons who are yet to acquire permanent resident status.","fn_6bd3568c":"The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","fn_737b31bd":"The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","fn_774ec898":"Venezuelans displaced abroad refers to persons who have left Venezuela as a result of the deteriorating circumstances inside the country, but who have not applied for asylum in the country in which they are present. As indicated in the Guidance Note on International Protection Considerations for Venezuelans (May 2019), UNHCR considers that the majority of Venezuelan nationals or stateless persons who were habitually resident in Venezuela, are in need of international protection under the criteria contained in the Cartagena Declaration on the basis of threats to their lives, security or freedom resulting from events that are seriously disturbing public order in Venezuela. In line with the Secretary General’s Guidance, UNHCR and IOM have been coordinating closely to respond to the outflow of Venezuelans.","fn_79b06469":"The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","fn_9bb6294a":"Refugees includes people in a refugee-like situation","fn_a61fe6dd":"Venezuelans displaced abroad refers to persons who have left Venezuela as a result of the deteriorating circumstances inside the country, but who have not applied for asylum in the country in which they are present. As indicated in the Guidance Note on International Protection Considerations for Venezuelans (May 2019), UNHCR considers that the majority of Venezuelan nationals or stateless persons who were habitually resident in Venezuela, are in need of international protection under the criteria contained in the Cartagena Declaration on the basis of threats to their lives, security or freedom resulting from events that are seriously disturbing public order in Venezuela. In line with the Secretary General’s Guidance, UNHCR and IOM have been coordinating closely to respond to the outflow of Venezuelans.","fn_e5870d2b":"Naturalization figures refer to the admission of protected persons as permanent residents of Canada. End-year stock refers to protected persons who are yet to acquire permanent resident status. The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment. Updated figures for the number of Ukrainians within the Canada-Ukraine authorization for emergency travel (CUAET) program have been reflected in the reported figure for people in a refugee-like situation.","fn_e7926654":"The statistics on asylum-seekers (new applications, re-opened/repeat applications and/or appeal application) and refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","fn_ec1068b6":"Naturalization figures refer to the admission of protected persons as permanent residents of Canada. End-year stock refers to protected persons who are yet to acquire permanent resident status. The statistics on refugees individually recognized in Canada include persons who had their claim assessed before the Refugee Protection Division and the Refugee Appeal Division of the Immigration Refugee Board as well as by the Department of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada through a Pre-Removal Risk Assessment.","fn_fb63bd8c":"End-year stock refers to protected persons who are yet to acquire permanent resident status."},"raw_files":{"persons_of_concern.csv":{"label":"UNHCR Refugee Data Finder download (persons_of_concern.csv)","header":["Year","Country of Asylum","Country of Origin","Country of Asylum ISO","Country of Origin ISO","Refugees","Asylum-seekers","IDPs","Other people in need of international protection","Stateless persons","Host community","Others of concern"]}},"raw_rows":{"persons_of_concern.csv#L102690":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":102690,"row":["2019","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","VEN","VEN","0","0","0","0","0","0","494503"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L103759":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":103759,"row":["2020","Canada","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","CAN","VEN","3524","1000","0","0","0","0","0"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L10723":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":10723,"row":["1996","Canada","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","CAN","VEN","546","0","0","0","0","0","0"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L108180":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":108180,"row":["2020","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","VEN","VEN","0","0","0","0","0","0","1112517"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L109273":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":109273,"row":["2021","Canada","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","CAN","VEN","4108","748","0","0","0","0","0"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L113756":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":113756,"row":["2021","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","VEN","VEN","0","0","0","0","0","0","1389980"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L114882":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line":114882,"row":["2022","Canada","Venezuela (Bolivarian Republic of)","CAN","VEN","1497","2104","0","0","0","0","0"]},"persons_of_concern.csv#L119696":{"file_key":"persons_of_concern.csv","line